  "comments": [
    {
      "position": 0,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "へ and に there is no difference. They can both be used and are considered interchangeable. I see both に and へ in writing and talking. \n\nSuch as:\n\nえきにいきます。- I'm going to the train station.\n\n へ can replace に and vice versa.",
      "html": "へ and に there is no difference. They can both be used and are considered interchangeable. I see both に and へ in writing and talking. <br/><br/>Such as:<br/><br/>えきにいきます。- I'm going to the train station.<br/><br/> へ can replace に and vice versa.",
      "credits_raw": "Sakuratree",
      "content_sha256": "209e5231c2e6ebc63a9e7332bc60d69ea89adc640989d8b03131b4eb4fe932ac",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 1,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "In theory へ is for movement in a direction, while に implies arrival at a specific destination.\n[or some such]. In practise there is very little difference.",
      "html": "In theory へ is for movement in a direction, while に implies arrival at a specific destination.<br/>[or some such]. In practise there is very little difference.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "a4b59a4f9f6a666b1e1d4c56e252d9105024ea7d37f0863b95122a338517b02e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "also used as a shortcut in email as in\n　　DCへ \n ->this part is to DC:",
      "html": "also used as a shortcut in email as in<br/>　　DCへ <br/> -&gt;this part is to DC:",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "2efb4c21202f3bc8e874e706a37528e60a946d5e35a39cbfcbda1a4b34cf6cb8",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "? it would be nice to get an explanation of difference between ni and he. \nロンドンに行く＝ロンドンへ行く\nロンドンでお会いしましょう？",
      "html": "? it would be nice to get an explanation of difference between ni and he. <br/>ロンドンに行く＝ロンドンへ行く<br/>ロンドンでお会いしましょう？",
      "credits_raw": "dc",
      "content_sha256": "5c33c39362ef49497c6c49b54416b65eeff8f56ff0a33530d308d15f514d551e",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "\"In motion constructions -ni and -e appear to have the same distribution [...]. The primary difference in distribution is that -ni may occur in other verbal contexts, as I show below, but -e may not, while -e may appear marking arguments in nominal constructions but -ni may not, [...]\"",
      "html": "\"In motion constructions -ni and -e appear to have the same distribution [...]. The primary difference in distribution is that -ni may occur in other verbal contexts, as I show below, but -e may not, while -e may appear marking arguments in nominal constructions but -ni may not, [...]\"",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "ad9f3c62098ce4cff54a57697c39c6d6a9986db1715b169187a46f3025df5c84",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "N = noun",
      "html": "N = noun",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "b6e11ae04b17d089e81475ac582765786990339e919a68bc606e0272521abcf0",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "Note: Apart from the \nDCへ \nletter / email addressing type usage you can't use へ to indicate going to a person.\ne.g. (BAD) DCへ行きました。[DC he ikimashita] I went to DC.\n(GOOD) DCの家へ行きました。[DC no ie he ikimashita] I went to DC's house.",
      "html": "Note: Apart from the <br/>DCへ <br/>letter / email addressing type usage you can't use へ to indicate going to a person.<br/>e.g. (BAD) DCへ行きました。[DC he ikimashita] I went to DC.<br/>(GOOD) DCの家へ行きました。[DC no ie he ikimashita] I went to DC's house.",
      "credits_raw": "Amatuka",
      "content_sha256": "cf8f226e55a5add0a1d4d4840c85c0eb17be6a3bc9336671461f025b4f7946c6",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    },
    {
      "position": 7,
      "source_id": null,
      "text": "I'd get rid of the above 'bad' example, because DC is also a place (Washington DC), in which case you CAN say \"DCへ行きました。\" Put some other person's name in that to make your point, and then please delete this comment :)",
      "html": "I'd get rid of the above 'bad' example, because DC is also a place (Washington DC), in which case you CAN say \"DCへ行きました。\" Put some other person's name in that to make your point, and then please delete this comment :)",
      "credits_raw": "Anon",
      "content_sha256": "918294162e37db781d1506f4f4a08656133f5e4c93678dddee730b9b24bce1d5",
      "original_created_at": null,
      "original_updated_at": null
    }
  ],
